second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who replaced Saint-Pierre-à-Champ in their role?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 85, \"text\": \"**HEADLINE:** French Commune Merger: Saint-Pierre-à-Champ Absorbed into Val en Vignes\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 87, \"end\": 107, \"text\": \"**DATE:** March 2019\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 109, \"end\": 337, \"text\": \"In a move aimed at streamlining local governance and improving public services, the French commune of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ has officially been replaced by Val en Vignes, a commune in the Deux-Sèvres department of western France.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 338, \"end\": 519, \"text\": \"According to official records, the merger was finalized on January 1, 2019, as part of a nationwide effort to consolidate rural communes and enhance their administrative efficiency.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 520, \"end\": 674, \"text\": \"This move marks a significant shift in the region's administrative landscape, with Val en Vignes now serving as the primary governing entity for the area.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 675, \"end\": 802, \"text\": \"\\\"We are thrilled to welcome the residents of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ into our community,\\\" said Val en Vignes Mayor, Pierre Dupont.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 803, \"end\": 912, \"text\": \"\\\"This merger will enable us to pool our resources, reduce costs, and provide better services to our citizens.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 913, \"end\": 951, \"text\": \"It's a win-win for everyone involved.\\\"\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 952, \"end\": 1174, \"text\": \"Data from the French National Institute for Statistics and Economic Studies (INSEE) reveals that Saint-Pierre-à-Champ had a population of just 541 residents as of 2016, making it one of the smallest communes in the region.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1175, \"end\": 1302, \"text\": \"In contrast, Val en Vignes boasts a population of over 2,000 residents, providing a more sustainable base for local governance.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1303, \"end\": 1519, \"text\": \"\\\"The merger will allow us to maintain our rural way of life while benefiting from the economies of scale that come with being part of a larger community,\\\" said former Saint-Pierre-à-Champ Mayor, Marie-France Garnier.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1520, \"end\": 1618, \"text\": \"\\\"We're excited to work together with our new neighbors to build a brighter future for our region.\\\"\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1619, \"end\": 1757, \"text\": \"The merger is part of a broader trend in France, where rural communes are facing declining populations and increasing financial pressures.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1758, \"end\": 1905, \"text\": \"According to a report by the French Senate, over 1,000 communes have merged since 2015, with many more expected to follow suit in the coming years.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1906, \"end\": 2067, \"text\": \"As the dust settles on this latest merger, residents of Val en Vignes and former Saint-Pierre-à-Champ are looking forward to a new era of cooperation and growth.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2068, \"end\": 2161, \"text\": \"With a stronger, more unified community, the region is poised to thrive in the years to come.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 20, \"text\": \"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 22, \"end\": 115, \"text\": \"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was a former commune in France that existed until the late 19th century.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 116, \"end\": 255, \"text\": \"According to historical records, the commune was replaced by the city of Paris in a series of events that took place between 1870 and 1880.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 256, \"end\": 269, \"text\": \"Early History\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 270, \"end\": 283, \"text\": \"-------------\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 285, \"end\": 370, \"text\": \"Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was founded in the 12th century as a small agricultural village.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 371, \"end\": 484, \"text\": \"The commune grew steadily over the centuries, becoming a significant center for trade and commerce in the region.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 485, \"end\": 598, \"text\": \"By the 18th century, Saint-Pierre-à-Champ had become a thriving town with a population of over 5,000 inhabitants.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 599, \"end\": 638, \"text\": \"The Replacement of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 639, \"end\": 675, \"text\": \"------------------------------------\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 677, \"end\": 821, \"text\": \"In the late 19th century, the French government embarked on a series of urbanization projects aimed at modernizing the country's infrastructure.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 822, \"end\": 953, \"text\": \"As part of this effort, the government decided to expand the city of Paris, which had become a major hub for industry and commerce.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 954, \"end\": 1148, \"text\": \"Studies conducted by the French Ministry of Urban Planning in the 1860s revealed that the expansion of Paris would require the absorption of surrounding communes, including Saint-Pierre-à-Champ.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1149, \"end\": 1344, \"text\": \"The study, led by French urban planner Baron Haussmann, concluded that the incorporation of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ into Paris would provide a significant boost to the city's economy and population.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1345, \"end\": 1456, \"text\": \"In 1875, the French National Assembly passed a law authorizing the annexation of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1457, \"end\": 1587, \"text\": \"The law was met with resistance from the residents of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ, who feared the loss of their autonomy and way of life.\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1588, \"end\": 1693, \"text\": \"However, the government ultimately prevailed, and the commune was officially absorbed into Paris in 1880.\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1694, \"end\": 1703, \"text\": \"Aftermath\"}, \"D2S19\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1704, \"end\": 1714, \"text\": \"----------\"}, \"D2S20\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1716, \"end\": 1809, \"text\": \"The replacement of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ by Paris had significant consequences for the region.\"}, \"D2S21\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1810, \"end\": 1962, \"text\": \"The absorption of the commune led to a significant increase in population and economic activity in Paris, cementing its status as the capital of France.\"}, \"D2S22\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1963, \"end\": 2071, \"text\": \"However, the loss of autonomy and identity for the residents of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ was a significant blow.\"}, \"D2S23\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2072, \"end\": 2157, \"text\": \"Many residents chose to leave the area, leading to a decline in the local population.\"}, \"D2S24\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 2158, \"end\": 2378, \"text\": \"Today, the area that was once Saint-Pierre-à-Champ is a thriving neighborhood in Paris, but the memory of the former commune lives on as a testament to the complex and often contentious history of urbanization in France.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Val en Vignes\", \"scope\": \"French commune\", \"claim\": \"The French commune of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ has officially been replaced by Val en Vignes.\", \"answer\": \"Val en Vignes\", \"quote\": \"In a move aimed at streamlining local governance and improving public services, the French commune of Saint-Pierre-à-Champ has officially been replaced by Val en Vignes, a commune in the Deux-Sèvres department of western France.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Val en Vignes\", \"Paris\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Val en Vignes\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Paris\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"Pierre Dupont\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"Marie-France Garnier\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}, {\"id\": \"C4\", \"answer\": \"Baron Haussmann\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}]}"
